Another question I had is for the storage slot tree key derivation why not have storage keys after the header start at the `MAIN_STORAGE_OFFSET` rather than `MAIN_STORAGE_OFFSET + HEADER_STORAGE_OFFSET` i.e. changing the `get_storage_slot_tree_keys` function to:

```python
def get_storage_slot_tree_keys(storage_key: int) -> [int, int]:
    main_offset: int = HEADER_STORAGE_OFFSET + storage_key
    if main_offset < CODE_OFFSET:
        pos = main_offset
    else:
        pos = MAIN_STORAGE_OFFSET + main_offset - CODE_OFFSET
    return (
        pos // 256,
        pos % 256
    )
```

This would allow 256 keys (`[64; 320)`) to be stored together in the same sub-tree instead of only having the next 192 storage keys in the first main storage sub-tree
